// OTD-0017 - SIS key switch in PROGRAM mode
// Library: OT Threat Content  |  Legacy ID: OT-UC-0017
// ATT&CK for ICS: T0858  |  Severity: Critical
// Detection logic: Detects a force/override flag being set on a tag belonging to the Safety Instrumented System (SIS) address range, a technique directly associated with the TRITON/TRISIS attack against a Schneider Electric Triconex SIS controller.
//
// STATUS: SCAFFOLD. This detection is catalogued as a specification; the logic below
// expresses the intent against the mapped table but MUST be completed and validated
// against real telemetry before deployment. Placeholders in <angle brackets> are
// environment-specific.
//
OTNozomi_CL
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
// TODO: express the detection condition -- Detects a force/override flag being set on a tag belonging to the Safety Instrumented System (SIS) address range, a technique directly associated with the TRITON/TRISIS attack against a Schneider Electric Triconex SIS controller.
| where isnotempty(SourceIP)
| summarize Count = count(), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated)
    by SourceIP, DestinationIP
| where Count > <THRESHOLD>
| order by Count desc
